  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 11,
  "Question": "If \\(\\log_2(\\log_2(\\log_2(x)))=2,\\) then how many digits are in the base-ten representation for \\(x?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(7\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\)",
    "E": "\\(13\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The definition \\(\\log_2 u=v\\) means \\(u=2^v\\). Apply this definition to the outermost logarithm first, then repeat:\n\\[\n\\log_2(\\log_2 x)=2^2=4,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\log_2 x=2^4=16,\n\\]\n\\[\nx=2^{16}=65536.\n\\]\nThe logarithm arguments at this value are \\(65536\\), \\(16\\), and \\(4\\), all positive, so every logarithm is defined. The number \\(65536\\) has \\(\\boxed{5}\\) decimal digits, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
